            "review_title": "Review at Bonjour Resto' Hai Ba Trung",
            "review_text": "gwlj\nFort Lauderdale, Florida55 contributions\n0\nCertainly better than other reviews here\nFeb 2020 • Couples\nHave searched for French restaurants in this former colony and disappointed in the lack there of. Have eaten here twice, nice rack of lamb, little over cooked for my taste, but typical of this culture. Wonderful French fries. Second visit, the duck was ok. Friend’s beef was good. Compared to the one star competitors (l’Etoile) across the main street, this place is Maxims. Staff is efficient and got the job done. english OK. Only beer is Heineken, which I don’t understand the French connection. Otherwise a good local beer is preferable to me. Busy place on ground level. Second floor empty. Toilet on the second floor was not a great inconvenience. 5000 dong for a napkin is a rip off, but I guess if they do it and locals let them get away with it, so be it. Life in the big city. Give it a try if small portions of a reasonable attempt at French at a fair price with salad or vegetable and potato included is your thing.\nRead more\nWritten February 16, 2020",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-15",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
